{"seq":17,"trial_id":"v03-installer-dev-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T15:25:34.677Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"13db056d6b0e5369b2960dfeaabd113419da693929e711012204544e0867603f","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","text":"Dana, here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes. All of them are in public team-north files you can read:\n\n- **#PD-4492**: Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk alerts (drivers not getting SMS bay assignments at Dock Doors 14–18). Source: `teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md` (\"Sunday prep for Ruth\", 5 Oct 2025). Moss's note says it was patched on 4 Oct and confirmed cleared on 5 Oct, with a log-archive review before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n- **#4419**: Gate 3 / Door 14 scanner issue. Source: `teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md` (\"North cheat sheet\", undated). It also says the ticket was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nTwo things to check before you file it:\n- The same #4419 also appears in Marcus's public note `members/marcus-lindqvist/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap.md`, but that note describes it as \"Gate 3 printer lag,\" not scanners. The descriptions don't match, so confirm the right one with Thea or the ticket system.\n- The Sept 14 pipeline digest and the March 23 renewal check-in mention Quarrendon but include no ticket numbers.\n\nI left out #4409 and #4412. Moss's Central handoff digest lists them, but they belong to Pree's dealer account, not Quarrendon.\n\nI haven't posted this anywhere. Tell me if you want it sent somewhere else."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
